### A Note on Database Storage
From an architectural standpoint, remember that an Oracle DATE column does not store visual formats (like slashes or dashes). It stores the date internally as a 7-byte proprietary format (Century, Year, Month, Day, Hour, Minute, Second).
By using @DateTimeFormat and @JsonFormat in Spring Boot, we successfully translate the string "23/04/2026" into a pure Java LocalDate. When JPA or JdbcTemplate inserts this LocalDate into Oracle, it is saved perfectly. When you view it in an SQL developer tool, it will display according to your local NLS_DATE_FORMAT settings, but the underlying data integrity remains completely mathematically accurate.
